Package: chanprobe
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: bidirectional audio channel prober for half duplex radio links
 chanprobe measures the amplitude and phase response of a half duplex audio
 channel from 150 Hz to 10.5 kHz, in both directions, using an extension of
 the ITU-T V.34 line probing signal (60 tones on a 150 Hz grid).
 .
 Two stations exchange tones, probe signals and their measurements (sent with
 the codec2 FreeDV DATAC1 OFDM data modem), then both display the relative
 amplitude, phase anomaly and per-tone SNR, plus the noise floor, the sample
 clock offset and the continuity of the audio (dropouts, sample slips). The
 two sides may run at 44.1 or 48 kHz. The transmitter is keyed through Hamlib.
